Sval: a popup takes its menu backdrop when only its appearance changes

nsMenuPopupFrame::GetShadowStyle() reads the appearance as well as
-moz-window-shadow, and the window shadow style decides the system
backdrop a macOS popup gets (setEffectViewWrapperForStyle). But
DidSetComputedStyle sends the shadow style to the widget only when
-moz-window-shadow changes, so a popup whose appearance changes from
none to menupopup keeps the plain view it was made with, and shows what
is behind it without the menu's material. Firefox's panels that Sval
draws as popovers change their appearance this way as they open in a
see-through window.

diff --git a/layout/xul/nsMenuPopupFrame.cpp b/layout/xul/nsMenuPopupFrame.cpp
index 6293a170d3..a7b2131ceb 100644
--- a/layout/xul/nsMenuPopupFrame.cpp
+++ b/layout/xul/nsMenuPopupFrame.cpp
@@ -513,6 +513,8 @@ void nsMenuPopupFrame::DidSetComputedStyle(ComputedStyle* aOldStyle) {
   if (aOldStyle->StyleDisplay()->EffectiveAppearance() !=
       StyleDisplay()->EffectiveAppearance()) {
     flags += WidgetStyle::MicaBackdrop;
+    // GetShadowStyle() depends on the appearance too.
+    flags += WidgetStyle::Shadow;
   }
 
   const auto& pc = *PresContext();
